content:
We propose ROS-SLAM-Hospital, a novel approach to integrate Cartographer-based mapping, AMCL localization, and a lightweight sensor fusion middleware for odometry correction. The proposed software module is designed to prioritize loop-closure robustness, reduce spurious map artifacts, and provide deterministic planning latency. The main contributions of this work are:

1) A hospital-focused SLAM integration framework combining Lidar, RGB-D, IMU, and wheel odometry, validated on an onboard Jetson + STM32 platform;
2) A detailed hardware and communication design for deployment at Wongsonegoro Hospital, including power distribution and network topology;
3) Extensive experiments in real hospital corridors quantifying map IoU $95.4\%$, localization RMSE $0.12\ \mathrm{m}$, and planning latency $12.3\ \mathrm{ms}$, surpassing baselines;
4) Open procedural guidelines for routine map updates and remote monitoring suitable for hospital IT integration.
